===persian===

به چتر درختی ایمن پناه برده ام و... مرا خواب در ربوده است
از صدای دور دارکوبی بیدار میشوم
خش خشی میشنوم
تو از درختان انبوه
به دریا می روی
جنگل بستری ست از برگهای رنگین
با صدای انفجاری... از جا میپرم...
جنگل پر از همهمه میشود.
هواپیماها میرند.
تو هیچ نمی ترسی...
به آغوش من پناه می آوری
بوی برگها... بوی خاک...
طعم دريا... و عطر نفس های تو...
پرندگان جنگل خاموش اند....
آفتاب رفته است....
و من با پر سبز دارکوبی
بر پشت چشمان بسته ات سایه میزنم

تابستان ۱۳۶۶

===machine===

I have taken refuge in the safe shade of a tree and... sleep has taken hold of me.
I wake up to the distant sound of knocking.
I hear rustling.
You are from the thick trees
You go to the sea
The forest is a bed of colorful leaves.
With an explosive sound... I jump up...
The forest is filled with noise.
Planes go.
You are not afraid of anything...
You take refuge in my arms
The smell of leaves... the smell of soil...
The taste of the sea... and the scent of your breath...
The birds of the forest are silent.
The sun has gone...
And I, with a green feather, am a woodpecker.
I cast a shadow behind your closed eyes.

Summer 1366

===lantern===

I've taken refuge under the safe canopy of a tree, and... sleep has carried me off.
I wake to the far knocking of a woodpecker,
I hear a rustling:
you, through the crowded trees,
are walking down to the sea.
The forest is a bed of colored leaves.
At the sound of an explosion... I spring up...
the forest fills with clamor.
The planes pass over.
You are not afraid at all —
you take shelter in my arms.
The smell of leaves... the smell of earth...
the taste of the sea... and the scent of your breathing...
The birds of the forest have fallen silent...
the sun has gone...
and I, with a woodpecker's green feather,
draw a soft shade across your closed eyes.

Summer 1366

